---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import ProcessPipeline from "../components/ProcessPipeline.astro";
import { sitePath } from "../site-path";
---

<SiteLayout
  title={"VietJusticIA platform · Ace Nguyen"}
  description={"The university computing project behind VietJusticIA, including a Vietnamese legal assistant, mobile document lookup and a lawyer portal."}
  bodyClass="case-study-page"
>
  <main id="main" class="project-page">
    <section class="case-intro wrap" aria-labelledby="case-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">University final project · May-December 2025</p>
        <h1 id="case-title">VietJusticIA<span class="blue">.</span></h1><p class="case-deck">Building a Vietnamese legal-assistance platform.</p></div>
      <div class="case-context"><p>I built a mobile app for people asking legal questions and a web portal for the lawyers answering consultation requests. My computing project focused on getting the interfaces, document retrieval and live conversations working together.</p>
        <dl><div><dt>Platform</dt><dd>React Native mobile app and React web portal</dd></div><div><dt>My work</dt><dd>Application development with substantial AI-assisted code generation</dd></div></dl></div>
    </section>
    <nav class="chapter-nav wrap" aria-label="Project sections"><a href="#mobile">Mobile app</a><a href="#answer-flow">Answer flow</a><a href="#portal">Lawyer portal</a><a href="#development">Development</a></nav>
    <section class="wrap chapter" id="mobile">
      <div class="chapter-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Mobile app</p><h2>Finding the source behind an answer.</h2></div>
      <div class="chapter-prose">
        <p>A reader can ask a question in Vietnamese or search the legal library by title. The library also supports filters such as document type, issuing body and status.</p>
        <p>Source entries with a document ID open the same reader from chat. The reader shows the full text, metadata such as the document number and status, and links to related documents when available.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="audit-gallery">
        <figure>
          <a class="evidence" href={sitePath("assets/work/audit-menu.webp")} aria-label="Enlarge navigation menu">
            <img src={sitePath("assets/work/audit-menu.webp")} width="439" height="848" alt="Navigation menu with Vietnamese entries for legal lookup and contacting a lawyer." loading="lazy">
          </a>
          <figcaption>Navigation menu</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <a class="evidence" href={sitePath("assets/work/audit-reader.webp")} aria-label="Enlarge legal document reader">
            <img src={sitePath("assets/work/audit-reader.webp")} width="440" height="886" alt="Vietnamese resolution with two columns of official headings above the article text." loading="lazy">
          </a>
          <figcaption>Legal document reader</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <a class="evidence" href={sitePath("assets/work/audit-verification.webp")} aria-label="Enlarge verification screen">
            <img src={sitePath("assets/work/audit-verification.webp")} width="440" height="848" alt="Invalid verification code alert displayed over the code entry dialog." loading="lazy">
          </a>
          <figcaption>Account verification</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="structure" id="answer-flow"><div class="wrap chapter">
      <div class="chapter-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Legal answer pipeline</p><h2>From a question to its sources.</h2></div>
      <div class="chapter-prose"><p>FastAPI saves each question and its reply in MongoDB, along with the source references. Each retrieval run uses the latest message. The saved history lets readers revisit earlier answers and reopen their sources.</p></div>
      <ProcessPipeline label="VietJusticIA legal answer pipeline" steps={[
        { label: "Ask", title: "Vietnamese question", description: "The mobile app sends a question to the authenticated chat endpoint." },
        { label: "Find", title: "Keyword and vector search", description: "The backend segments the Vietnamese text and combines results from BM25 and Qdrant." },
        { label: "Expand", title: "Parent passages", description: "The service uses each match’s parent ID, when present, to fetch a longer passage for context." },
        { label: "Answer", title: "Gemini and sources", description: "Gemini drafts a reply from the passages. The backend matches the model’s source titles to document records." },
      ]} />
      <p class="flow-note">If the backend can’t match any source titles from the model, it lists the retrieved passages as references instead.</p>
      <div class="flow-details" aria-labelledby="index-heading">
        <h3 id="index-heading">How the search index is built</h3>
        <p>The backend splits legal text from MongoDB into larger passages for context and smaller excerpts for BM25 search. Each excerpt records the ID of its parent passage.</p>
        <p>A separate script embeds excerpts with a multilingual sentence model and writes them to Qdrant. It uses its own text splitter and omits the parent IDs. A vector result from that script can’t supply a parent passage on its own.</p>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="wrap chapter" id="portal">
      <div class="chapter-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Lawyer portal</p><h2>Taking a request into a conversation.</h2></div>
      <div class="chapter-prose"><p>A person selects an available lawyer in the mobile app and sends a request from their profile. The lawyer reviews it in the portal. Once accepted, both participants can read the conversation history and reply.</p>
      <p>Administrators have a separate workspace to manage users and legal documents. Keeping those tasks in the web portal leaves the mobile experience focused on the person asking for help.</p></div>
      <ProcessPipeline label="Lawyer conversation flow" steps={[
        { label: "Request", title: "Choose a lawyer", description: "The app sends the request to the selected lawyer. It appears as pending in their portal." },
        { label: "Accept", title: "Open the conversation", description: "Accepting the request automatically creates a conversation linked to it." },
        { label: "Talk", title: "Stay in sync", description: "The backend saves messages in MongoDB and uses WebSockets for new messages, typing indicators and read receipts." },
      ]} />
    </section>
    <section class="wrap chapter" id="development">
      <div class="chapter-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Development</p><h2>Connecting the pieces.</h2></div>
      <div class="chapter-prose"><p>I used FastAPI for the backend, Qdrant for document retrieval and WebSockets for chat. The repository includes the mobile app, the React and TypeScript portal, and Playwright tests covering login, administration and lawyer conversations.</p>
      <p class="project-actions"><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/npqace/vietjusticia">Explore the code on GitHub</a></p></div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <footer class="footer wrap"><a href={sitePath("vietjusticia.html")}>Read the mobile redesign</a><a href={sitePath("#work")}>All work</a></footer>
</SiteLayout>
